    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Cloud Platforms for ML: Where Should Your Model Run?\"\ndescription: \"VMs, serverless containers, Kubernetes and managed ML platforms on AWS, Google Cloud and Azure, with an interactive cost calculator and a traffic simulation.\"\nauthor: \"MLStation\"\ndate: 2026-10-01\ncategories: [Deployment, Cloud, AWS, GCP, Azure]\ndraft: false\n---\n\nPayGuard is now a container. The next question is **where it lives**. Every cloud offers the same basic menu at different levels of \"how much do you want to manage yourself\". The right choice depends mostly on **traffic shape, team size and budget**.\n\n::: {.callout-tip}\n## What you will learn\n- The four ways to run a model in the cloud, from raw servers to fully managed ML\n- The matching services on AWS, Google Cloud and Azure\n- How always-on servers and pay-per-request pricing compare, with a calculator\n- Free options for small projects\n:::\n\n::: {.callout-note appearance=\"simple\"}\n## The Deployment series\n**Start:** [1. Overview: from notebook to production](/deployment/deployment-overview.qmd)\n\n**Build:** [2. Tools](/deployment/tools/ml-serving-tools.qmd) · [3. MLOps](/deployment/mlops/mlops-pipelines.qmd) · [4. Docker and containers](/deployment/containers/docker-for-ml.qmd) · [5. Cloud and platforms](/deployment/cloud/cloud-platforms-for-ml.qmd)\n\n**Operate:** [6. Scale](/deployment/scale/scaling-ml-inference.qmd) · [7. Monitoring](/deployment/monitoring/model-monitoring-drift.qmd) · [8. Maintenance](/deployment/maintenance/ml-model-maintenance.qmd) · [9. Updates and versioning](/deployment/update/model-versioning-rollouts.qmd)\n:::\n\n\n## Who manages what\n\nMoving from left to right, the provider takes over more of the work. You gain convenience and lose some control. Pick a level to see the split.\n\n```{ojs}\n//| echo: false\nimport {ms, msStyle} from \"/assets/js/ms-plot.js\"\nlevels = [\"Virtual machine\", \"Kubernetes\", \"Serverless container\", \"Managed ML platform\"]\nviewof lvl = Inputs.radio(levels, {value: \"Serverless container\", label: \"Run on\"})\n```\n\n```{ojs}\n//| echo: false\n{\n  const stack = [\"Model and code\", \"Endpoint and scaling rules\", \"Container runtime\", \"Autoscaling\", \"Operating system and patches\", \"Servers and network\"];\n  const yours = {\"Virtual machine\": 6, \"Kubernetes\": 4, \"Serverless container\": 1, \"Managed ML platform\": 1};\n  const n = yours[lvl], W = 760, h = 38;\n  const notes = {\n    \"Virtual machine\": \"Full control, full responsibility. Good for steady traffic and custom setups.\",\n    \"Kubernetes\": \"The cluster runs many services. Powerful, but needs platform skills.\",\n    \"Serverless container\": \"Push a container, get a URL. Scales to zero when idle.\",\n    \"Managed ML platform\": \"Training, registry, endpoints and monitoring in one product.\"\n  };\n  return htl.html`<div>${htl.svg`<svg viewBox=\"0 0 ${W} ${stack.length * (h + 6) + 30}\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:${W}px;font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif\">\n    ${stack.map((s, i) => htl.svg`<g>\n      <rect x=\"10\" y=\"${i * (h + 6)}\" width=\"${W - 20}\" height=\"${h}\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"${i < n ? ms.indigo : ms.teal}\" fill-opacity=\"${i < n ? 0.85 : 0.25}\"/>\n      <text x=\"30\" y=\"${i * (h + 6) + h / 2 + 5}\" font-size=\"13.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"${i < n ? \"white\" : \"currentColor\"}\">${s}</text>\n      <text x=\"${W - 30}\" y=\"${i * (h + 6) + h / 2 + 5}\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"${i < n ? \"white\" : \"currentColor\"}\">${i < n ? \"You\" : \"Cloud provider\"}</text></g>`)}\n  </svg>`}<div class=\"ms-readout\"><span>${lvl}</span><b style=\"font-size:1rem\">${notes[lvl]}</b></div></div>`;\n}\n```\n\n## The same menu on three clouds\n\n| What you need | AWS | Google Cloud | Azure |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Virtual machines | EC2 | Compute Engine | Virtual Machines |\n| Serverless containers | App Runner, Lambda (container images) | Cloud Run | Container Apps |\n| Managed Kubernetes | EKS | GKE | AKS |\n| Managed ML platform | SageMaker AI | Vertex AI | Azure Machine Learning |\n| Object storage for models | S3 | Cloud Storage | Blob Storage |\n| Container registry | ECR | Artifact Registry | Container Registry |\n\n: Equivalent services across clouds {#tbl-clouds}\n\nAmazon's ML platform is now called **Amazon SageMaker AI** ([AWS](https://aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/ai/)). The concepts carry across clouds, so learning one makes the others easy.\n\n## Traffic shape decides the bill\n\nMost models are not busy all day. Below is a simulated week of PayGuard traffic for a small online shop: busy evenings, quiet nights, a weekend peak.\n\n::: {#cell-fig-traffic .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code code-fold=\"true\"}\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd, plotly.graph_objects as go\nfrom ms_charts import COLORS, PLOTLY_CONFIG\nrng = np.random.default_rng(21)\nt = pd.date_range(\"2026-09-07\", periods=7 * 24 * 60, freq=\"min\")\nh = t.hour + t.minute / 60\ndaily = 4 + 30 * np.exp(-((h - 20) ** 2) / 8) + 12 * np.exp(-((h - 12.5) ** 2) / 3)\nweekend = np.where(t.dayofweek >= 5, 1.5, 1.0)\nrpm = rng.poisson(daily * weekend)\npeak = np.percentile(rpm, 99.5)\nhourly = pd.Series(rpm, index=t).resample(\"15min\").mean()\nfig = go.Figure()\nfig.add_scatter(x=hourly.index, y=hourly.values, fill=\"tozeroy\", name=\"Requests per minute\",\n                line=dict(color=COLORS[\"indigo\"], width=1.5), fillcolor=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.25)\")\nfig.add_hline(y=peak, line_dash=\"dash\", line_color=COLORS[\"rose\"], annotation_text=\"Always-on server sized for peak\", annotation_position=\"top left\")\nfig.update_layout(height=360, yaxis_title=\"Requests per minute\", showlegend=False)\nfig.show(config=PLOTLY_CONFIG)\nutil = rpm.mean() / peak\n```\n\n::: {#fig-traffic .cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:360px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5